An unlock that hands a mutex to its oldest waiter without putting it on the waiter's ring.
The new holder could not give it back at its destroy, nor borrow through it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a held mutex is missing from its holder's ring

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -652,7 +652,6 @@ static struct thread *mutex_give(struct mutex *m)
         w->flags &= (uint8_t)~THREAD_LENDS;
         w->frame.regs[REG_A0] = KERR_OK;
         m->holder = v2p(w);
-        held_push(w, m, mutex_lends(m));
     }
     /* Only a mutex that lent was the one its holder borrowed from, the first. */
     if (lent) {
